{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers","id":1554563,"title":"Explaining Thin Blooded prejudice to newcomers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-22T14:29:25-07:00","id":1554563,"title":"Explaining Thin Blooded prejudice to newcomers","content":"I'm trying to have several older Kindred explain it and varying reasons. Also, how much of it should exist in your games.<br /> <br /> Here's my first answer:<br /> <br /> Racism.<br /> <br /> There's reasons for the racism like the fact that they're too human-like to really empathize with, endanger the Masquerade, and are too easily killed to really be useful. Some vampires even have religious reasons like they're portents of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> But at heart, most vampires despise Thin Bloods because they're weak and easy to bully around. Which ironically means most Thin Bloods have no problem selling out older vampires to the Second Inquisition or using their small powers to fuck up older Kindred.<br /> <br /> They also are near-universally Anarchs, which doesn't give the Anarchs much of a boost until you remember that they can still use guns and molotovs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T16:23:26-07:00","id":1554569,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is the best answer.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't really empathize with other vampires, at least no more than they empathize with mortals. And as far as power and usefulness goes, they're better than Ghouls, but still less liked. If power and being easily bullied were the main points, clan vampires would actually like Thin-Bloods more than they like other vampires.<br /> <br /> The game always relied heavily on fear for this prejudice. Vampires fear Thin-Bloods, for a number of reasons:<br /> <br /> 1- Strange powers. Thin-Bloods (and Caitiff) develop powers other vampires can't. For creatures that thrive in control and knowledge, this level of unpredictability is a horrible thing. You don't know what they're capable of, and that's worse than knowing they're capable of more potent tricks than you. You can prepare against potent tricks you know how to work and what they do;<br /> <br /> 2- You don't know shit about them. Even if the origins of vampirism aren't really know despite legends, overall it's a predictable phenomenon. You know how things work and how they relate. And then comes a bunch of people that defy everything you though you know. Their nature, their powers, why they're so different, nothing about them really fits with how vampires work in general. And you never know when you'll find a new shocking difference between them and other vampires (like the development of TB Alchemy);<br /> <br /> 3- Most have a degree of resistance to sunlight and holy things, the greatest limitations of vampires. Nothing strikes fear in a Kindred's heart more than the risk of being attacked during daysleep, when they're the most vulnerable, and Thin-Bloods are foes with powers and knowledge about the vampire condition other hunters don't have. Worse, most vampires get even more useless during the day as time passes, so this completely flips expectations as powerful elders will be the most diminished vampires if taken by day;<br /> <br /> 4- Legend plays a huge role here. That has always been the greatest point in the lore: Camarilla elders fear the Thin-Blood because their dismissal of Gehenna is a facade. Thin-Bloods are actually welcomed in some domains, and the less a vampire believes in the Book of Nod, the more likely they are to welcome Thin-Bloods, to the point where in many domains persecuting them became a bad, unpopular policy. With 5th edition making the Camarilla turn 180\u00ba on the Noddist stance, now it's even more likely that in Cam domains the Thin-Bloods will be formally hunted.<br /> <br /> All that said, their ability to provide new services through TB Alchemy does means a lot of vampires may now reevaluate their stance on TBs as they're more directly useful. But ongoing Gehenna, as anti-climatic as it got to be, adds complexity to the problem. For some this is proof that the fear was warranted and they must be destroyed, or things will get worse. For others this is proof that they had nothing to do with that, or at least that they're not a problem anymore, we're already screwed, so let them be. Not to say that not everyone even believes Gehenna is ongoing, or will ever happen.<br /> <br /> Prejudice is a complicated thing. A lot of it doesn't have to do with perceived inferiority, but with perceived threat. Great Replacement Theory, innate savagery, bad omens, Conspiracy Theories. Jews, Blacks, Latinos, we're not victimized because people see us as inferior, despite stating this is a part of how we're victimized. We're victimized because people see us as a threat for completely ludicrous reasons. Of course there are far more complexity to RL prejudice (specially structural prejudice), but that's the gist of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T17:14:25-07:00","id":1554572,"title":"","content":"Adding to monteparnas's points<br /> <br /> -the masquerade. Yes I know, it's the main excuse of the Camarillo and others to exterminate the thin blood, but it's not utterly baseless.<br /> <br /> A large art of what allows the masquerade is the fact that due to their curses and their nature, vampires are constantly reminded of how they're no longer the same as humans.<br /> <br /> Thin blood have a far weaker version of that perceptual barrier. They can live easier in the daytime, some have relatively normal metabolism, some can even have children. For such thin blood. The separation from humans is far more of a belief than an absolute fact, hence they will be more tempted to be more represent with their friends and family, and worse, they might consider a world where they can reveal themselves to humans.<br /> <br /> -diablery. Devouring another kindred is something every single vampire might be tempted to do, but no one has more incentives to do so than thin blood. Even a 12 generation vampire might be content of his powers, and th k the risk of amarakth too much of a rice for he benefits, but ea thin blood is weak. Even in a society where they were not treated like vermin or second class citizen, their lack of strength would make them lacking compared to others. Worse, many will never be able tovemprzce, so the only way to bring their favored mortal into the night might be to first drain your ventrue neighbor.<br /> <br /> Furthermore on the last point, thin blood are a constant reminder that diablery is a necessity for the vampire race to exist. After all, your potential to create a perennial line is limited by your generation, there will I inevitably be a time where your descendant will be thin blooded and incapable of embracing. And as lower generations vampire can be killed, the only way for the species to endure is when the youngest east the oldest, ensuring their own chance to perpetuate kindred into the coming nights.<br /> <br /> So seeing thin bloods in your city is an eternal reminder that despite the apparence of eternity, your own species is degrading generation and generation, constantly perpetuating the tendancy tovdiaboery, and therefore the fear of the young. In many way, seeing one of them is telling you that the war of ages will never, ever stop","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 10-22-2025, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T17:44:04-07:00","id":1554575,"title":"","content":"An exemple of that in game happened in one of my campaigns.<br /> <br /> We were in a French city under a pseudo Camarilla regime (I was using the omega conspiracy plot line, with all PCs being of bloodlines rather than clans), the city had a population of thin blood which whose presence were tolerated and which were protected from direct discrimination (although of course, this being Vtm, this was not with good intentions). <br /> <br /> The players quickly interacted with them and became friends with Emilie and Patrocle, two thin blood acting as de facto leader/protective older siblings of the thin bloods. The first issues appeared quickly, the thin blooded were afforded the freedom to deal with their own stuff as long as they didn't cause trouble. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBut vampire being vampires, they were some skirmishes with criminals, suspicions from detectives and vigilantes, and I'll timed feeding that resulted in corpses. But the thin blood had a far lower threshold of abilities than full blooded kindred, so they couldn't just memory wipe witnesses, they couldn't as easily physically outmatch the local brutes trying to impose their turf limits, and they couldn't just blood bond their local tenants to avoid weird questions on their nocturnal lives. Hence the interventions of the PCs to set things right. <br /> <br /> Howether, after a time, weird occurrences happened, thin bloods disappeared alongside other kindred, the former quickly accused the full bloods of eliminating them, then the blame was put on the mysterious threat looming over the city which is the current main plot of the campaign. <br /> <br /> In reality, as the PCs ended up discovering, the thin bloods were kidnapping kindred, then diablerised them. The newly ascended kindred then hid to avoid being known as diablerists, and the group was simply wondering whenether it would be best to leave the city in order to find new preys (which they cynically referred as &quot;unwitting level ups&quot;) or whenether to wait until they're suffiently numerous and strong to take over the city at large. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T17:55:58-07:00","id":1554576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554569#post1554569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is the best answer.<br /> The game always relied heavily on fear for this prejudice. Vampires fear Thin-Bloods, for a number of reasons:</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course:<br /> <br /> 5- It's obvious to vampires, especially older vampires, that Thin-Bloods won't want to stay thin-blooded forever. Thin-Bloods are weaker than actual vampires, and the power structure of vampiric society is designed to prop up actual full fledged vampires. This naturally pushes Thin-Bloods towards engaging in diablere, meaning that every Thin-Blood is a diablerist that simply hasn't committed diablere just quite yet. But they will, all of them eventually will if you give them half the chance. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T18:40:35-07:00","id":1554580,"title":"","content":"Apparently the anti spam system swallowed my first comment, so here it is again<ul><li>Adding to monteparnas's points<br /> <br /> -the masquerade. Yes I know, it's the main excuse of the Camarilla and others to exterminate the thin blood, but it's not utterly baseless.<br /> <br /> A large part of what allows the masquerade is the fact that due to their curses and their nature, vampires are constantly reminded of how they're no longer the same as humans. Hence most won't even think to try to be with humanity. <br /> <br /> Thin bloods have a far weaker version of that perceptual barrier. They can live easier in the daytime, some have relatively normal metabolism, some can even have children. For such thin blood. The separation from humans is far more of a belief than an absolute fact, hence they will be more tempted to be more represent with their friends and family, and worse, they might consider a world where they can reveal themselves to humans.<br /> <br /> -diablery. Devouring another kindred is something every single vampire might be tempted to do, but no one has more incentives to do so than thin blood. Even a 12 generation vampire might be content of his powers, and that the risk of amaranth too much of a rice for he benefits, but a thin blood is weak. Even in a society where they would not be treated like vermin or second class citizen, their lack of strength would make them lacking compared to others. Worse, many will never be able tovemprzce, so the only way to bring their favored mortal into the night might be to first drain your ventrue neighbor.<br /> <br /> Furthermore on the last point, thin blood are a constant reminder that diablery is a necessity for the vampire race to exist. After all, your potential to create a perennial line is limited by your generation, there will I inevitably be a time where your descendant will be thin blooded and incapable of embracing. And as lower generations vampire can be killed, the only way for the species to endure is when the youngest east the oldest, ensuring their own chance to perpetuate kindred into the coming nights.<br /> <br /> So seeing thin bloods in your city is an eternal reminder that despite the apparence of eternity, your own species is degrading generation and generation, constantly perpetuating the tendancy tovdiaboery, and therefore the fear of the young. In many way, seeing one of them is telling you that the war of ages will never, ever stop<br /> Last edited by Nyremne; Today, 07:19 PM</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T01:32:36-07:00","id":1554589,"title":"","content":"I think everyone said basically everything already so I am a bit late to the party<br /> But nonetheless I Will throw my own two coppers in the pile<br /> Thin Bloods make things fall apart<br /> It is hard to pinpoint, but the fact is, Cainite Society built on several things and one of it is a shared and more-or-less agreed origin Clan Book: Settite Revised hit the head on the nail with that one<br /> <br /> &quot;The other vampires' shared name of &quot;Cainite&quot; is the first and greates lie. They base their myth on the Biblical account of Cain(e)m whom God cursed for murder of his brother Abel. According to the Cainites, this curse was nothing less than to become the First Vampire. Caine passed on his Curse to others mortals, who passed it in turn to several more. These wretches, in turn, sired all the various breed of vampires. I must you shall recignize the inconsistencies in this myth. Eternal life makes, shall we say, a peculiar punishment for a murderer. Forcing him to consume blood and thos repeat his crime again and again is idiotic.Making the curse transmissible to innocent people snacks of pure madness. To explain the differences among various breeds of vampires, the myth complicates itself with accounts that Caine himself cursed various Antediluvians for ill-defined offenses, and that these curses transmitted themselves to the Foudners' descendants. The legends go on to speak of a &quot;First City&quot; established by Caine; a Second City of the Antediluvians, the biblical Deluge, wars, and various catastrophes provoked by crimes against Sires. Self-proclaimed Cainite scholars waste rivers of ink exploring and explaining they cycle of myths. Waste, I say, because our most ancient temples in Egypt preserves eyewitness accounts of the myth's genesis. Not all these accounts come from members of our divine lineage, The Legend of Caine, the First Vampire dates back no earlier then 2000 BC. A cabal of Elder Vampires (millenia old even then and possibly including some of the 'Antediluvians') concocted this spurious shared inheritance. This was part of an attempt to regiment their rebelious descendants - hence the repeated warning of dire punishments for disobeying one's elders. They tried to create an early version of the Camarilla, though with little success.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Thin Bloods the embodiment of the &quot;lie&quot; falling apart<br /> <br /> Also they embodiment fear - fear that comes from the realization Cainites are a de-facto &quot;dying breed&quot;<br /> <br /> If one hate Thin Blood based on relegious/Nodist reason they do it because:<br /> <br /> &quot;And you will know these last times by the Time of Thin Blood, which will mark vampires that cannot Beget, you will know them by the Clanless, who will come to rule\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> Elders and other Kindred - even if the Camarilla has never openly declared their belief in Noddism, the Antediluvians (and stangely deny their existance while most of them really proud of their lienage and sometimes even require you to list your line up to the foudner\u2026 that never really existed\u2026?) use this a justification for hunting down Thin Bloods and Caitiff<br /> While they ready to ignore the fllowing lines that are basically just a dozen lines under the &quot;warning&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Beware those who walk without a clan, for they will be our undoing.<br /> Pity them! Adopt the orphans where you can.<br /> But watch them. In them is the bad seed of their Sire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention - tho this is something the vampires rarely aware if they are not knee deep in Nodism - the whole &quot;Curses of Caine&quot; really only was given to Caine and his descendants<br /> <br /> This is funny, really because:<br /> <br /> Michael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> Raphael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth,you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always. Hide now for the Sun rises to take its wrath on you.&quot;<br /> Uriel cursed him: \u201eThen, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness! You will drink only blood. You will eat only ashes. You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on. You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Not even died, but cursed to live on: &quot;You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not God per see who cursed him (or depends, thrugh the Archangels God expressed his Will)<br /> And more importantly, not even not died, when he recieved the curses... was an immortal basically, living in the darkness, eating ash and blood.<br /> But technically, in theory totally capable to reproduce normally Thus Caine had a mortal &quot;family&quot; and potentially passed the curse (&quot;for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children) to these Humans (As a side side note, Genesis 4:17 tells us, \u201cCain knew his wife, and she conceived and bore Enoch.\u201d That is the first and last mention of the wife of Cain in the entire Bible. Naturally, this raises some questions: Who was she, and where did she come from?<br /> I would really love to take a deep dive in the theory and evidances of a pre-Adamic race and Caine's mortal line and their effects on Vampire, but then this post would be two miles long, but if any interested\u2026<br /> ...so moving on!)<br /> <br /> And then the Demons showed him how to Embrace:<br /> <br /> &quot;He saw within his blood the potence of fertility By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom He learned the way to make a child for his own.&quot; - Book of Nod<br /> <br /> Uriel gave him a warning and just to be sure, a little curse-extention: &quot;Caine, though powerful you are, and marked of God, know you this: that any Childe you make will bear your curse, that any of your Progeny will forever walk in the Land of Nod, and fear flame and sun, drinking blood only and eating ashes only. And since they will carry their father's jealous seed, they will forever plot and fight amongst themselves. Doom not those of Adam's grandchildren who seek to walk in righteousness. Caine! Stay your dread Embrace!&quot; But he decided to went along anyway\u200b&quot;<br /> Making not one but two potentially cursed and breed of Humans/undead<br /> <br /> Erciyes Fragments says that Caine levied a curse on the Third Generation after they killed their sires (excep probably the many - and I mean MANY direct Child of Caine, only MAYBE Irad is the one that bit the dust\u2026) - to make each generation weaker than the last.<br /> One of the Cainite scholars providing running commentary says that diablerie existed before then, but was largely just a perversion--it didn't make you more powerful, it just felt good.<br /> <br /> So, we have a basically infernal blood rite to trap the soul in a body after death to be a Vampire, passed down personal curses and a few of Caine's own that resuled in a dying race of undead who are progressively weaker to the point their curses are so weak they can give birth, eat, barely or non able to use the powers in the vitae and even the Sun us not that deadly<br /> <br /> This breeds fear and a horrific realisation - if it is true, they are dying out<br /> If you are a Cainite who knows his Book of Nod, Revelations of Dark Mother, Erciyes Fragments, Shaal Fragments, Prague Plaques, Shroud of Kaymakli and various other sources and you belive them?<br /> Then the Thin Bloods are a frightening proof your are done for and have a tons of misguided reasons to hate them<br /> <br /> If you are a run-of-the mill Cainite?<br /> You hate Thin-Bloods and Caitiff because:<br /> <br /> - Everyone else does<br /> - They have no-one to stand up for them and you can feel &quot;stronger&quot; , be a bully and feel good becasue they can't fight back, no one will protects them and they are beneath you. Yay. <br /> - You are jealous of their lack of a curse and chains<br /> <br /> <br /> As a final joke, Time of Thin Blood basically confirmed prophecy about the Thin Bloods essentially self fulfilling or ironic one.<br /> <br /> Basically what really wakes the Antediluvians is the shedding of large amounts of cainite vitae.<br /> So by hunting and destroying the Clanless as a &quot;sign of the end times&quot; the Elders are actually hastening Gehenna, which effectively makes the prophecy correct because the clanless did doom the kindred<br /> BUT not by existing...<br /> ...but by being destroyed.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T08:13:29-07:00","id":1554594,"title":"","content":"I have a number of comments to make here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;23890&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadeprowler[/USER] ]It is hard to pinpoint, but the fact is, Cainite Society built on several things and one of it is a shared and more-or-less agreed origin</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't completely agree, especially before <i>Revised</i>, but even then.<br /> <br /> Noddism is an important element in the game, and its influence is certainly a powerful trope. As I said before, legend plays a huge role.<br /> <br /> But their society isn't really built on this. Most of how and why it works has only to do with pragmatism and politics.<br /> <br /> Even though Generation and Ancients are important themes for the game, their <i>cause</i> isn't. How they came to be is irrelevant to how they built vampire society.<br /> <br /> <i>Players</i>, not the actual game, gave a lot of weight to the legends that exist within the setting. Not that the books can't be blamed for this misunderstanding, but it's a misunderstanding nonetheless.<br /> <br /> What I can agree, overall, is that too many Elders believe those legends, and their belief is important because they act on it. But everything works just fine when local Elders don't believe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;23890&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadeprowler[/USER] ]Beware those who walk without a clan</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Those who walk without a clan&quot; aren't the <b>Thin Bloods</b>, but the <b>Caitiff</b>.<br /> <br /> But it's good to remember that many (not all) of the things that can be said in this thread about the <b>Thin Bloods</b> also apply to the <b>Caitiff</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;23890&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadeprowler[/USER] ]But technically, in theory totally capable to reproduce normally</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a number of interesting things that may be done with this take, by the way.<br /> <br /> Revenants may have been Caine's mortal descendants all along. Maybe the Tzimisce just found them out, never really &quot;created&quot; them. And other families may exist independently.<br /> <br /> Maybe there is a small but extant race of Dhampyrs descended from Caine. They may use rules for Revenants, for Dhampyrs, for Thin Bloods, or a mix thereof. They may even be mostly normal vampires that just don't Embrace, a Bloodline that's either hidden or, even more interesting, secretly be a well known Bloodline or even Clan. Or some <b>Caitiff</b> may have the Blood of Caine, even be his direct children, that &quot;Self-Embrace&quot; at some point in life and can't remember it.<br /> <br /> An important note for anyone doing this: if Caine could have normal children, it also means he still <u>can</u>. Even because Caine isn't as much an actual First Vampire, if the Book of Nod is real, but a <b>thing</b> that's the forefather of vampires.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;23890&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadeprowler[/USER] ]If you are a Cainite who knows his Book of Nod, Revelations of Dark Mother, Erciyes Fragments, Shaal Fragments, Prague Plaques, Shroud of Kaymakli and various other sources and you belive them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably don't exist in the first place.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that characters don't have all the access players have. Those sources are hard to find and read, and mixed with a lot of junk (either falsifications or just bad translations/editions).<br /> <br /> A lot of what was presented to us in the many, many books, comes from the perspective of a character that read an &quot;original&quot; fragment, so to speak. Most vampires, even elders intended on researching the subject, never had the opportunity, much less for every single information given.<br /> <br /> So your regular vampire actually has the short version of the modern legend and a few pieces of random (and incorrect/incomplete) trivia. Elders usually have a lot more trivia, but if they're not dedicated scholars of Noddism (and most aren't) that's about it. Elder scholars may have got the chance to know something closer to our OoC knowledge, but peppered with junk and mostly fifth-hand accounts at best, with a few opportunities to read a fragment now and then if they're well enough connected.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always decide that in your game Beckett published the ultimate book on Noddism and now anyone with an interest may be that informed, but this is not standard to the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;23890&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadeprowler[/USER] ]If you are a run-of-the mill Cainite?</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have 3 other fear-based reasons to fear <b>Thin Bloods</b> without any worry about Gehenna.<br /> <br /> And you possibly still fear them because of Gehenna, there's no need to actually know a lot of Noddist lore.<br /> <br /> I still think that if you don't fear them, then they're too good a resource to hate them.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T10:18:42-07:00","id":1554598,"title":"","content":"Mind you, the people destroying Thin Bloods for religion are being incredibly stupid because the idea of killing a sign of Gehenna to thwart it is stupid logic even by prophecy standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T11:01:36-07:00","id":1554600,"title":"","content":"I think that in part it's tied to the reason why having children out of wedlock was such a taboo through out most of history and why &quot;bastard&quot; was a pretty dire insult and bastards were in fact mistreated.<br /> <br /> It has to do with important values that maintain social cohesion and the taboo against actions that undermine those values. Traditionally, in human cultures, marriage and monogamy was a large part of the glue that bound society together, not just the family unit but inheritance, gender roles, child care, and so one. People who had children who weren't married undermined that social order and so a huge amount of stigma was associated with that - for the children and their parents, especially mothers.<br /> <br /> For vampires and thin blooded vampires, including caitiffs, there is something similar. We get both thin blooded vampires and/or caitiffs when vampires are embracing too quickly and too frivolously. Vampires shouldn't be abandoning their progeny, they should be getting permission from the prince/elder to embrace, high generation vampires shouldn't get such permission. The more frivolous embraces that happen, the more likely we are to have more thin blooded vampires and caitiffs. Also, lots of embraces like this are likely to shift power in the direction of the young, which also threatens the stability of the elder based hierarchy.<br /> <br /> There are, of course, religious objections to thin blooded vampires - but the secular Camarilla has thin blooded vampires as do many largely secular elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T14:20:55-07:00","id":1554603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554598#post1554598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, the people destroying Thin Bloods for religion are being incredibly stupid because the idea of killing a sign of Gehenna to thwart it is stupid logic even by prophecy standards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if there's a prophecy of the end of the world and you know prophecies have actual potency, it would be rational to do everything to stop it's signs from appearing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T14:55:40-07:00","id":1554607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554603#post1554603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, if there's a prophecy of the end of the world and you know prophecies have actual potency, it would be rational to do everything to stop it's signs from appearing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's not much of a prophecy then, is it? 3000 years ago, we had stories about how those kind of efforts only screw you over.<br /> <br /> See Oedipus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:01:10-07:00","id":1554609,"title":"","content":"My Malkavian's character answers.<br /> <br /> Fear:<br /> <br /> Our kind believes that the Thin Bloods are a sign of our end times as we have been taught that's it is a sign of our end times where our potent blood gets weaker and weaker with each generation and for them to gain greater power is consume us older and stronger generations.<br /> <br /> Racism: There is always going to be members of our society that will be looked down upon as inferior and my clan is no stranger to it.<br /> <br /> Envy: The Thin Bloods are closer to humanity and they are a reminder of what we have lost over the ages and have a chance to regain there lives. I've been undead for over a 150+ years and I wouldn't remember all the things that made us mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T17:05:43-07:00","id":1554622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554607#post1554607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it's not much of a prophecy then, is it? 3000 years ago, we had stories about how those kind of efforts only screw you over.<br /> <br /> See Oedipus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, as far as we know, oedipus is just a story made up by humans in the wod. <br /> <br /> While kindred have exemple of actual oracle's. So the opinion of human mythology on the future would not be much of a consideration for beings who might actually know a prophet or two. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, that's exactly how prophecies seems to work in the WOD, they have criteria that, if met, will lead to the promise outcome. In fact that's exactly how it works according to transylvania chronicle. With saulot twisting &quot;when here will be massacres of thin blood&quot; (paraphrasing) to &quot;there will be load of thin blood&quot; with the goal that kindred, feared the fake sign, would eliminate thin bloods, hence triggering the actual sign, which is what tin fact happens in the storyline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T18:45:22-07:00","id":1554626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554598#post1554598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, the people destroying Thin Bloods for religion are being incredibly stupid because the idea of killing a sign of Gehenna to thwart it is stupid logic even by prophecy standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but people aren't logical most of the time.<br /> <br /> Add to this that characters have, I'll say it again, incomplete, incoherent and adulterated information, that they don't even know if it's real to begin with.<br /> <br /> So a lot of interpretations about what this sign means are possible, and the idea that it is something the community should act upon isn't rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554563-explaining-thin-blooded-prejudice-to-newcomers?p=1554607#post1554607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it's not much of a prophecy then, is it? 3000 years ago, we had stories about how those kind of efforts only screw you over.<br /> <br /> See Oedipus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, again, that's not really how prophecies work.<br /> <br /> Myths aren't prophecies <i>per se</i>. They're stories. Prophecies are open to interpretation and frequently talk about things people can act upon.<br /> <br /> How you interpret a prophecy is half the prophecy, and it's always a gamble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T18:26:12-07:00","id":1554706,"title":"","content":"To add further on Prophecies in a storyteller venue, every story I've read is usually the characters bring about the very events they sought to prevent. Be it Cable from the X-Men, the Alederai in Warhammer when they sought to edit the future and so on. So Monteparnas is right that acting on one is fraught with unseen risks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T12:06:26-07:00","id":1554862,"title":"","content":"I suspect the explanation boils down to:-<br /> <br /> - All vampires are rivals<br /> <br /> - These rivals are weaker than **** near everybody<br /> <br /> - Therefore let us rid ourselves of them, for they will weaken us until and unless they get fed into OUR grinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}